From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libheal: include engine types before inline accessors

License: GPL-3.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: downstream-only
Origin: openEuler RISC-V packaging

The optional libheal target compiles imageSynth.c separately.  That translation
unit includes mapIndex.h and adaptSimple.h, whose inline functions use Pixelel
and Coordinates, without first including the headers that define those types.
The normal plugin engine happens to establish that order in engine.c, so the
problem was hidden while libheal and its functional harness remained disabled.

Include the two type headers before map.h and the inline accessors.  This is the
same dependency order already used by engine.c and changes no runtime logic.

Remove this patch when upstream's libheal target provides the type definitions
before mapIndex.h and adaptSimple.h, or registers an equivalent maintained test
target that supersedes testHealLib.

---
 lib/imageSynth.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/imageSynth.c b/lib/imageSynth.c
--- a/lib/imageSynth.c
+++ b/lib/imageSynth.c
@@ -46,6 +46,8 @@
 #include "glibProxy.h"  // glibProxy.c
 
 #include "imageFormat.h"
+#include "engineTypes2.h"
+#include "coordinates.h"
 #include "imageFormatIndicies.h"
 #include "map.h"  // header for mapOps.h included by engine.c
 #include "engineParams.h" // engineParams.c
